From 228f0281996c1dc33cc59998d083c3d172044e44 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Youll <andrewyoull86@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 12:40:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] avcodec: h264_vchiq, H.264 decoded by the Raspberry Pi's
 VideoCore (RISC OS)

The VideoCore's own H.264 decoder, driven from RISC OS through the VCHIQ
module and the firmware's MMAL service by vcdec (riscos-reelhwaccel's
libvcdec). Packets go to it as Annex B access units with their pts (the
h264_mp4toannexb filter for MP4); pictures come back in display order
and are copied into ordinary YUV420P frames. receive_frame only waits
for the VideoCore when its input is full or at the end of the stream; a
flush is a seek (after the end of the stream vcdec creates the decoder
again, so nothing is lost).

Streams the VideoCore can't take (profiles other than Baseline, Main and
High, 10-bit or 4:2:2, over 1920x1088, 1080p with gpu_mem under 128 MB,
no VCHIQ) are refused at open with AVERROR(ENOSYS), so a player can use
the h264 decoder instead. It is not the default H.264 decoder: ask for
it by name (-c:v h264_vchiq).

--enable-vchiq (GPL), needs vcdec.h and libvcdec.
Options: sync_receive, gpu_mem_check.
---
 configure              |   6 +
 libavcodec/Makefile    |   1 +
 libavcodec/allcodecs.c |   1 +
 libavcodec/vchiqdec.c  | 405 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 413 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 libavcodec/vchiqdec.c

